In article <1990Jul30.172225.26679@wam.umd.edu> hawthorn@wam.umd.edu (Ian James Hawthorn) writes:
>A cursed ring of hunger is self explanatory - you don't want to wear one for
>very long. What do you do with it once you have finally de-cursed the thing
>however? Consider the following.
If I understand the ring of hunger correctly, you use it in between Troll
snacks to lose the "satiated" attribute more quickly until you eat your
next Troll.  Of course, a tinning kit is better.
>#5: A cursed -2 ring of strength
Useful when you have a character whose to-hit probability is so high that
he/she cannot hit at all (presumably because it has wrapped around
to zero).  This happened to me with a +100 longsword and all 18 stats
with Gauntlets of Power.  I could hit Liches and other nasties with no
problem but I could *never* get a hit in on a Goblin.  If anybody can
get a +100 longsword without being in Wizard mode, let me know!
